+// A4-declared Excel sheets printed in Letter mode (owner decision 2026-11-14: follow the Office reference). Excel paginates the sheet ON A4 and scales every A4 page onto
+// the Letter page. Calc lays the sheet out exactly as on A4 (100 %: the same rows and columns on each page, the same cell text layout) and the PDF export draws that A4
+// page scaled and shifted onto a Letter page: getRenderer reports the Letter page size and a "ScWasmPageTransform" property that filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx applies
+// to the PDF writer's map mode. (An earlier version scaled through the page style's zoom: Calc's integer zoom of 91 to 95 % laid some wrapped cell text out one line
+// shorter and a line was lost.) A no-op unless LO_WASM_A4_LETTER_MAPPING is "1" (the bridge sets it for a PDF target with Letter paper) and the document came from an Excel filter.
+struct PageTransform
+{
+    double fScale = 1.0, fOffsetX = 0.0, fOffsetY = 0.0;           // 1/100 mm on the Letter page
+    tools::Long nContentWidth = 0, nContentHeight = 0;              // the A4 content area, 1/100 mm
+    tools::Long nPageWidth = 0, nPageHeight = 0;                    // the Letter page, 1/100 mm
+};
+SC_DLLPUBLIC bool GetA4LetterPageTransform(ScDocument& rDoc, tools::Long nWidth, tools::Long nHeight, PageTransform& rOut);
 }
 
